<figure class="lms-figure" aria-labelledby="fig-refund">
  <figcaption id="fig-refund" class="lms-figure-caption">Void or refund? It depends on the batch</figcaption>
  <div class="lms-fork">
    <div class="lms-fork-branch">
      <p class="lms-fork-title">Batch still open (same day)</p>
      <p class="lms-fork-verb">Void</p>
      <ul class="lms-fork-list"><li>Cancels the sale before it is ever sent.</li><li>No fee, nothing settles.</li><li>The hold on the customer's card drops off in a few days; nothing “comes back” because nothing left.</li></ul>
    </div>
    <div class="lms-fork-branch">
      <p class="lms-fork-title">Batch already closed</p>
      <p class="lms-fork-verb">Refund</p>
      <ul class="lms-fork-list"><li>A new transaction that sends money the other way.</li><li>Fees on the original sale are usually not returned to us.</li><li>Shows on the customer's statement in roughly 5–14 days, set by their bank.</li></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</figure>
